<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Datacenter-Gpu on Best of AI</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tags/datacenter-gpu/</link><description>Recent content in Datacenter-Gpu on Best of AI</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://bestofai.io/tags/datacenter-gpu/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Intel Crescent Island</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/intel-crescent-island/</link><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/intel-crescent-island/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Intel gave a deep technical rundown of its Crescent Island inference GPU at Hot Chips 2026 in August, following up its earlier disclosure of the chip. It packs 32 Xe3P cores, 256 XMX matrix engines, and 32MB of unified L2 cache, and leans on capacity-dense LPDDR5X rather than HBM: the standard air-cooled card ships with 160GB at 350W, with ODM designs supporting up to 480GB for customers who need to fit larger models without a memory-bandwidth-first design. Intel is targeting AI inference and agentic workloads specifically, trading some raw throughput for lower power and higher memory capacity per card. Customer sampling is expected in the second half of 2026, with a full launch slated for 2027.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Microsoft Maia 200</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/microsoft-maia-200/</link><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/microsoft-maia-200/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Microsoft unveiled Maia 200 in January 2026 as the successor to its first in-house Maia 100 chip, moving from TSMC&amp;rsquo;s 5nm node to 3nm and packing 144 billion transistors. It carries 216GB of HBM3e memory at 7 TB/s of bandwidth plus 272MB of on-chip SRAM, and delivers around 10 petaflops of FP4 and 5 petaflops of FP8 compute within a 750W envelope, with native FP8/FP4 tensor cores tuned for inference rather than training. Microsoft says it offers roughly 30 percent better performance per dollar than the prior generation. At Hot Chips 2026 in August, Microsoft gave its deepest public look yet at the chip&amp;rsquo;s architecture as it prepares to deploy Maia 200 across Azure data centers.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Rebellions Rebel100</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/rebellions-rebel100/</link><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/rebellions-rebel100/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AMD Instinct MI430X</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi430x/</link><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi430x/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AMD Instinct MI440X</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi440x/</link><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi440x/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AMD Instinct MI455X</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi455x/</link><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi455x/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Huawei Ascend 950DT</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/huawei-ascend-950dt/</link><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/huawei-ascend-950dt/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AMD Instinct MI100</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi100/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi100/</guid><description/></item><item><title>AMD Instinct MI210</title><link>https://bestofai.io/hardware/amd-instinct-mi210/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:0